1,"language":"Java","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":6031,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":634,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":6031,"open_issues":634,"watchers":21911,"default_branch":"release-v2","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"- ExoPlayer 2.12.2\r\n- Android 11 (R)\r\n\r\nIn Android 11 the next error is shown in the logcat:\r\n\r\n```\r\nTried to access visual service WindowManager from a non-visual Context:app.application.App@35e268c Visual services, such as WindowManager, WallpaperService or LayoutInflater should be accessed from Activity or other visual Context. Use an Activity or a Context created with Context#createWindowContext(int, Bundle), which are adjusted to the configuration and visual bounds of an area on screen.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe problem is originated from the fact that in the ExoPlayer **MediaCodectVideoRenderer** class constructor, the context is resolved as the application one:\r\n\r\n`this.context = context.getApplicationContext();`\r\n\r\nFull logcat stacktrace:\r\n\r\n```\r\nE/ContextImpl: Tried to access visual service WindowManager from a non-visual Context:app.application.App@35e268c Visual services, such as WindowManager, WallpaperService or LayoutInflater should be accessed from Activity or other visual Context. Use an Activity or a Context created with Context#createWindowContext(int, Bundle), which are adjusted to the configuration and visual bounds of an area on screen.\r\n    java.lang.IllegalAccessException: Tried to access visual service WindowManager from a non-visual Context:app.application.App@35e268c\r\n        at android.app.ContextImpl.getSystemService(ContextImpl.java:1914)\r\n        at android.content.ContextWrapper.getSystemService(ContextWrapper.java:803)\r\n        at com.google.android.exoplayer2.video.VideoFrameReleaseTimeHelper.<init>(VideoFrameReleaseTimeHelper.java:77)\r\n        at com.google.android.exoplayer2.video.MediaCodecVideoRenderer.<init>(MediaCodecVideoRenderer.java:255)\r\n        at com.google.android.exoplayer2.DefaultRenderersFactory.buildVideoRenderers(DefaultRenderersFactory.java:366)\r\n        at com.google.android.exoplayer2.DefaultRenderersFactory.createRenderers(DefaultRenderersFactory.java:310)\r\n        at com.google.android.exoplayer2.SimpleExoPlayer.<init>(SimpleExoPlayer.java:610)\r\n        at com.google.android.exoplayer2.SimpleExoPlayer$Builder.build(SimpleExoPlayer.java:513)\r\n        at app.ui.widget.video_player.SessionPlayback.<init>(SessionPlayback.java:97)\r\n        at app.ui.widget.video_player.VideoPlayerView.setMedia(VideoPlayerView.java:195)\r\n```\r\n\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8363/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/856265185","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8246#issuecomment-856265185","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8246","id":856265185,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg1NjI2NTE4NQ==","user":{"login":"jackmichalak","id":51389104,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzg5MTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51389104?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak","html_url":"https://github.com/jackmichalak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-06-07T21:20:16Z","updated_at":"2021-06-07T21:20:16Z","body":"Would love to see this addressed. Following through the stack trace it appears (at a quick glance) that replacing `context.getApplicationContext()` with just `context` in a half dozen or so places would allow the user-supplied Context to be utilized. What am I missing that makes this tricky?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/856265185/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jackmichalak","id":51389104,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzg5MTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51389104?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak","html_url":"https://github.com/jackmichalak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jackmichalak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/856692355","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8246#issuecomment-856692355","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8246","id":856692355,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg1NjY5MjM1NQ==","user":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-06-08T11:43:47Z","updated_at":"2021-06-08T11:44:29Z","body":"I agree it's quite straightforward for the common case of video playback in a single activity. However, there are some complications for other cases. For example, it's quite easy to accidentally leak an activity context with the suggested approach, particularly for use cases where playback may transition between activities, or be detached from an activity altogether (e.g., for transitioning into background playback). If the player is initially constructed for background playback, then the application may not have a suitable context to provide at construction time.\r\n\r\nMore generally, `VideoFrameReleaseTimeHelper` is making some assumptions about video being rendered on the default display. So far this has not caused any real issues that we're aware of, but the assumption itself is increasingly less likely to hold true as multi-display devices become more common. If such devices start to drive their displays in more flexible ways, the current implementation of `VideoFrameReleaseTimeHelper` could become more problematic in the future. The only use of `WindowManager` in `VideoFrameReleaseTimeHelper` is a line of code that makes such an assumption, so it might be that we should be making more substantial changes that will cause the need to retrieve it to disappear entirely.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/856692355/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/856728105","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8246#issuecomment-856728105","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/8246","id":856728105,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg1NjcyODEwNQ==","user":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-06-08T12:36:38Z","updated_at":"2021-06-08T12:37:52Z","body":"As a short term fix, it looks like we can just replace use of `WindowManager.getDefaultDisplay` with `DisplayManager.getDisplay(DEFAULT_DISPLAY)`. This doesn't solve any of the potential problems around multiple displays, but it does remove the warning whilst avoiding both (a) the need for plumbing changes outside of `VideoFrameReleaseTimeHelper`, and (b) increased risk of accidental context leaks. We'll go ahead and make that change.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/856728105/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"lau